<h1>Download Clients</h1>
<p class="page-meta">
  NGMS ships with embedded torrent and usenet engines. External clients are also supported.
</p>

<h2>Embedded engines (recommended for new installs)</h2>

<p>
  Both embedded engines are enabled from <strong>Settings → Download Clients → Embedded</strong>.
  No external process is needed — they run inside the NGMS binary.
</p>

<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Engine</th><th>Protocol</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Embedded Torrent</strong> (librtbit)</td>
      <td>BitTorrent</td>
      <td>Full BitTorrent client — DHT, PEX, piece selection, seeding, ratio rules</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Embedded Usenet</strong> (nzb-web)</td>
      <td>NNTP / NZB</td>
      <td>Downloads, yEnc decode, PAR2 repair, unrar — full pipeline in-process</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<div class="callout callout-tip">
  <span class="callout-icon">✦</span>
  <div class="callout-body">
    The embedded usenet engine requires NNTP server credentials — add them in
    <strong>Settings → Usenet Providers</strong>. The embedded torrent engine needs no
    additional credentials.
  </div>
</div>

<h2>External clients</h2>

<p>Go to <strong>Settings → Download Clients → Add</strong> and choose a client type:</p>

<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Client</th><th>Protocol</th><th>How NGMS connects</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>SABnzbd</td><td>Usenet</td><td>SABnzbd API — URL + API key</td></tr>
    <tr><td>NZBGet</td><td>Usenet</td><td>XMLRPC — host, port, username, password</td></tr>
    <tr><td>qBittorrent</td><td>Torrent</td><td>qBittorrent Web API — URL + credentials</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Deluge</td><td>Torrent</td><td>Deluge JSON-RPC — URL + password</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Transmission</td><td>Torrent</td><td>Transmission RPC — URL + credentials</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>Client priority and routing</h2>

<p>
  When multiple clients are configured, NGMS routes grabs by <strong>protocol</strong> first
  (usenet releases go to usenet clients, torrents to torrent clients), then by the
  <strong>priority</strong> order you set. Drag to reorder clients in the settings list.
</p>

<p>
  You can also assign a <strong>category</strong> per client — NGMS will tag each grab with
  that category so the external client can apply its own routing rules (e.g. different save
  paths per category).
</p>

<h2>Verifying a client works</h2>

<p>
  After saving a client, click <strong>Test</strong>. NGMS will attempt a connection and
  report any errors. Then do a manual search (series or movie → Search → grab a release) and
  verify it appears in the client's queue.
</p>

</DocsLayout>
